BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 512.10 Tm (gone. Tax Sale Secrets [GxMaS0YFT1Y @ 00:16:54] reports that historical imagery from 2004 to 2017 reveals) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 496.87 Tm (demolitions, after relying on plat maps for 20 years. Address errors compound it: Jason Porter [bnQAJL9-zo0 @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 481.65 Tm (00:00:52] watched Google pin the wrong address on a 2-bed, 1-bath property and refuses to trust the situs address until) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 466.42 Tm (the GIS confirms it, and Tax Sale Academy [Mp1_eOyha6A @ 00:01:20] warns that aerial angle can make the house) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 451.20 Tm (appear off its own lot because the lines are inexact. Skyler adds a mechanical failure, noting addresses can split when) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 435.97 Tm (pasted into search tools. Tax Sale Academy's Miami-Dade walk-through likewise compares 2005 imagery with current) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 420.75 Tm (aerials before a $35,000 opening bid. The fix is the redundancy the Rebels describe: parcel number into GIS, aerial plus) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 405.52 Tm (Street View history, then a second map source like Google Maps before the max bid is locked.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 390.30 Tm (Land is where practitioners report the most traps on cheap lists. Jason Porter [bnQAJL9-zo0 @ 00:01:27] found 1.14) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 375.07 Tm (acre parcels with $1,500 opening bids that looked worth $25,000 but sit underwater half the year, making them) Tj ET
