BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 406.30 Tm (The second trap is a judgment that does not hold. Casey Dimmon warns that a pro se filer who blows a single) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 391.07 Tm (stipulation can have the case thrown out by the judge. That burns hundreds of dollars in filing fees and hours of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 375.85 Tm (preparation. Worse, the filer can win a signed order whose language still fails the title insurance company's) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 360.62 Tm (requirements, which forces the whole process to start over [vMMozg0xaSA @ 00:04:02]. Darren Findlay calls the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 345.40 Tm (defendant list a net. Miss one fish, meaning one undischarged interest holder, and the judgment of quiet title does not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 330.17 Tm (resolve the title. The process then starts all over again just to get rid of that one party [kJRxvYeK_eU @ 00:03:19].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 314.95 Tm (Findlay says the office regularly gets called to fix judgments that other law firms obtained or started. The title company) Tj ET
